  "derivationRules": "Normal values come from the stage course's defaultConditions in courses.json; Hard values come from the stage's hard.variation in stages.json. (1) Surface-to-weather mapping, applied consistently: 'wet' surface pairs with weather 'rain'; 'damp' surface pairs with weather 'light-rain'; 'dry' pairs with 'clear' unless the text names a sky (overcast) or mist. (2) Named weather wins over rule 1: any text naming mist gives weather 'mist' (surface as stated, otherwise dry); 'light rain' gives damp/light-rain; 'steady rain' gives wet/rain. (3) A missing time of day inherits the Normal value for the same course; a missing surface is 'dry'. (4) Time words map as: 'late afternoon' -> late-afternoon, 'blue hour' -> blue-hour, 'clear evening' -> evening, 'early night' -> evening, 'moonlit night', 'cold night' and 'clear night' -> night, 'cold dawn' and 'clear dawn' -> dawn, 'first light' -> first-light. Adjectives such as 'cold' or 'moonlit' are kept in the Hard note only; they never imply ice or reduced grip. (5) C07 names no time of day; it uses 'night', matching the other Kasumi forest courses C05, C06 and C08. (6) C25 lighting progresses deterministically during the run without changing grip; timeOfDay records the start of the run and the optional 'progressesTo' field records the finish. (7) Hard entries whose variation names no condition change (S29) repeat the Normal conditions, and the note records the tightened targets.",
